# Transcript

Public transcripts of Audrey Tang’s speeches, interviews, and columns — roughly 2,000 Markdown files from 2015 to the present. They are released in the spirit of *publishing before perishing*: as soon as possible and open to correction by anyone.

Read them at [archive.tw](https://archive.tw), served by [sayit-hono](https://github.com/audreyt/sayit-hono).

For repository automation, validation, and agent-facing maintenance guidance, see [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

## File format

Each transcript is a standalone root-level Markdown document. Its filename carries the date and title:

```text
2026-03-04-Ciudadanía-Digital.md
2026-03-04-數位公民.md
```

The document begins with a title, then uses speaker labels and blockquotes to retain the structure of the original event:

```markdown
# 2026-03-04 數位公民

### 唐鳳：

（speech content）

> (Section Title)

（more content）

### 問：

（question text）

### 唐鳳：

（answer text）
```

- `# Date Title` — document heading
- `### Speaker:` — speaker label, such as `### Audrey Tang:` or `### 唐鳳：`
- `> (Section Title)` — section dividers, stage directions, or other non-speech context
- `### Question:` / `### 問：` — questions in Q&A sections

Older records reflect their source material and may vary slightly. When correcting a transcript, preserve its existing structure and wording unless the correction requires a change.

## Bilingual pairs

Many transcripts exist in English and Traditional Chinese. The `.alternates` file maps each pair with one tab-separated line:

```text
2026-03-04-Ciudadanía-Digital.md	2026-03-04-數位公民.md
```

This lets the publishing workflow send `alternate_filename` to the API so both versions are linked on the site.

## Publishing

```text
git push
    │
    ▼
GitHub Actions workflow
    ├─ sync changed transcripts and language pairs → archive.tw (D1 + R2)
    └─ rebuild the search index                  → deploy sayit-hono to Cloudflare Workers
```

On each qualifying push that changes a root-level transcript or `.alternates`, the workflow:

1. Detects added, modified, and deleted transcript files.
2. Detects language-pair changes and re-syncs affected records.
3. Uploads or deletes records through the archive.tw API, including `alternate_filename` for paired translations.
4. Rebuilds the Pagefind search index and redeploys the site.

## Contributing

If you spot an error, open a pull request. Keep corrections focused on the source record; the content is CC0 and may be corrected by anyone.

